PATCH 192: promote + reconstruct the 22dd mission-viewport handler at 0000:23f2.

The in-mission 22dd threaded-code interpreter (FUN_0000_22dd) dispatches its handlers through the cursor
`fist_icall_near(0, word[DGROUP:word[0x4a86]])`.  After patch 189 re-seeds the cursor to the mission
handler stream, the FIRST dispatched target is 0x23ea -- an engine MID-ENTRY Ghidra never promoted (it is
reached only through the 22dd handler-offset table, never by a direct call), so it missed the fmap and
fist_icall_near trapped it as a no-op -> the cursor never advanced (it re-dispatches 0x23ea forever, so the
main thread hangs in 22dd while the async op-0x4c present pump spins).  Confirmed live: FIST_TRACE_TRAPS=1
on the ACCEPT cascade logs `[icall] TRAP unmapped indirect call -> linear 0x023ea`.

0x23ea (`mov bx,0x6c34; jmp 0x23f2`), 0x23e5 (`bx,0x6c30`) and 0x23ef (`bx,0x6c2c`) are three mid-entries
into a shared body at 0x23f2 -- a fixed-point trig/normalise handler.  asm 0x23e5..0x2470 (verified vs
re_out/fist_dat_image.bin), DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00:
  ax=word[DG:bx]; dx=0; cl=byte[0x154a]; if(cl>1) dx:ax=ax*cl;          (scale)
  cl=0; normalise dx:ax to MSB-set (byte-shift-left-8 while dh==0, then bit-shift-left-1), cl=shiftcount;
  cl+=byte[0x154c]; ch=-(cl&0xf8); cl&=7; shr dx:ax by cl;              (align to exponent granularity)
  call 0xcbe (extract 16-bit mantissa->ax + byte-exponent->dx); dl+=ch; dl+=byte[bx+2];
  store ax->[0x6c26], dx->[0x6c28];                                     (the scaled/normalised coord)
  ax=word[0x1558]; call 0x5bc(cos)->[0x6c1e]/[0x6c20]; call 0x5b7(sin)->[0x6c22]/[0x6c24];
  call 0x374(octant)->[0x6c2a]; addw 2,[0x4a86].                        (advance the interpreter cursor)

Helpers 0xcbe (mantissa/exponent extract) and 0x374 (octant = ((-angle+0x4000) rol 3) & 7) are tiny
register-only transforms -> inlined faithfully (norm_cbe / oct_374).  The cos/sin wrappers 0x5bc/0x5b7
reuse the patch-157 sin-table core FUN_0000_05e2 for the mantissa (ax) and reproduce the wrapper's DROPPED
exponent word: 0x5e2 returns CF=1 (saturation, |value|==1.0) signalled by ax==0xffff, else CF=0; the
wrapper then sets dl=0xf0 (CF=0) or dl=0 (CF=1, with ax=1) and dh=cwtd sign of the arg passed to 0x5e2
(cos: word[0x1558]; sin: (-word[0x1558]) with +0x4000 to ah, i.e. cos of the 90deg-shifted angle -- 0x5b7
falls through into 0x5bc).  So dx = sign:0xf0 (normal) or sign:0x00 (saturation).

OBSERVATION GATE (per doctrine -- the fixed-point OUTPUT is not render-verifiable yet, the very next
handler 0x41d0 posts an op-0xc extender display-list record that is still a wall): with FIST_TRACE_TRAPS=1
on the cascade the trap moves FORWARD from linear 0x023ea to linear 0x041d0 -- i.e. the interpreter now
runs 23f2 to its `addw 2,[0x4a86]` and dispatches the NEXT handler.  Structurally asm-faithful.

Behaviour-neutral for the 19 verify flows: the handler is reached only through the d548-gated 22dd loop
(d548==0 in the menu, verified), and 0x23ea/0x23e5/0x23ef have no direct callers -- adding fmap entries +
new bodies cannot change any covered path.  verify.sh both stays 19/19; default boot rc=0; mainmenu md5
3a6ff1c5 unchanged.  Sources stay pristine (re_out/fist.c 61453e42); fist.c via build/.

